# Nothing in this file excludes deposit content. Every pattern here is either a
# build artifact or operating-system metadata, and MANIFEST_SHA256.txt covers
# every file git does track, .gitignore included.
#
# This file exists because make_manifest.py and git disagree about what to skip.
# make_manifest.py omits __pycache__ when walking, so a stray bytecode directory
# never enters the manifest - but git would commit it, publishing repository
# content the manifest says nothing about. That is the one failure the manifest
# cannot detect by construction, so it is prevented here instead.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Windows marks files copied from a download with an NTFS alternate data stream.
# WSL materializes those streams as real files, and seven of them were caught in
# this repository's first manifest run on 2026-10-02. make_manifest.py now
# refuses to write a manifest while any is present; this keeps them out of git.
*:Zone.Identifier
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

*~
*.swp
